{%- set paid = fightersAll | selectattr("support") | list %}
<div class="kicker"><a href="/">Follow the Money</a> · directory</div>
<h1>Pro-Democracy <em>Fighters</em></h1>
<div class="standfirst">The commentators, analysts, strategists, organizers, and organizations doing the work — {{ fightersAll | length }} of them, grouped by what they actually do.</div>
{%- if paid | length %}
<div class="fgt-legend">Everyone on this list has our support — that is what listing them <em>is</em>. The <span class="fgt-paid">$ money behind it</span> mark is narrower: it flags the {{ paid | length }} where we have also spent our own money, and says what on.</div>
{%- endif %}
<div class="hub-tagline">Know someone who belongs here? Tell us: contact@moralfibermedia.com</div>

{%- for group in fightersByCategory %}
<h2 class="fgt-cat">{{ group.name }} <span class="fgt-cat-n">{{ group.items | length }}</span></h2>
<div class="fighters">
{%- for f in group.items %}
  <a class="fgt{% if f.support %} is-paid{% endif %}" href="{{ f.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
    <span class="fgt-i">✊</span>
    <span><span class="fgt-n">{{ f.name }}</span>{% if f.support %}<span class="fgt-paid">$ {% if f.support is string %}{{ f.support }}{% else %}money behind it{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}<br><span class="fgt-d">{{ f.description }}</span><br><span class="ins-u">{{ f.display_url }}</span></span>
  </a>
{%- endfor %}
</div>
{%- endfor %}

